# Original Idea

`hark ssh-pair`: connect to another hark daemon running on a machine over ssh and act as a unified hark instance. should allow moving where TTS gets played, for example, and should optionally move the mic but not always because it might be wireless (as the user, record user preferences as natural language string somewhere, like `[config_dir]/nl_prefs/[preference-key-name].txt`). Goal is to make using hark at home seamless amongs multiple devices.

